#! /bin/python3.10
"""
ollamarun - a full `ollama run` wrapper with rendering and saved sessions

Version: 1.10

Summary of changes in this version:
  - The "loading MODEL…" line the background preload printed at session
    start is now the same animated dots spinner already used while waiting
    for a response mid-stream ("waiting for MODEL…"), instead of a plain
    static line -- reusing the existing widget rather than a one-off.
  - The background model preload now prints a "loading MODEL…" line as soon
    as the session starts, so there's a visible sign it's happening instead
    of the model silently warming up with no feedback. If a message is sent
    before that preload finishes, sending it now waits for that same load
    (instead of letting `/api/chat` kick off a second, redundant one), so
    `ollama ps` shows up right when the model becomes resident instead of
    only after the whole first response has finished generating.
  - Fixed the model's response being printed twice at the end of a stream:
    the live view's last frame could go stale (throttled refreshes may skip
    the final chunk), and the code used to paper over that by printing the
    whole rule + response a second time below it. It now forces one last
    live refresh before the live view freezes, so nothing is rendered twice.
  - `ollama ps` now prints as soon as the background-preloaded model finishes
    loading (typically while you're still typing the first message), instead
    of waiting until after the first response finished generating.
  - Model turns are now marked with a `rich` rule/divider instead of a full
    box, and the user/model chat colors are softer, muted pastel tones
    (was bold cyan/green) instead of the previous saturated colors.
  - The REPL now starts loading the session's model in the background as
    soon as the session opens, instead of waiting for the first message --
    it's already warming up while the user types. Pressing Enter on an
    empty line now sends immediately when there are pending images (e.g.
    from `/image PATH`), instead of being silently ignored, so attaching
    an image and hitting Enter with no text sends it for the model to
    process right away.
  - `/image` now parses its argument with shlex, so a quoted path
    (`/image "my photo.png"`) with spaces attaches correctly instead of
    being split into multiple bogus paths at each whitespace.
  - Split into a package. The implementation now lives in ollamarun_lib/
    (one module per pipeline stage: constants, helpers, mathrender, files,
    images, renderer, client, session, emit, interactive, repl, run, cli --
    see CLAUDE.md's Architecture section and each module's docstring) instead
    of one ~4300-line file. This script is now a thin entry point that adds
    its own directory to sys.path and calls ollamarun_lib.cli.main(). No
    behavior change; `ollamarun_lib` also re-exports every public name at
    the top level (`import ollamarun_lib as orun`) so existing callers and
    tests keep working unmodified.
  - Chat bubbles. User turns render as a small right-aligned box; model
    answers render inside a full-width box titled with the model name --
    live while streaming and in `/show`/`--show` transcript replays. Plain
    and raw render modes, and non-terminal output, are unaffected.
  - `/ps` shows the live `ollama ps` table (model, size, VRAM, quant,
    until-idle). The REPL also prints it automatically the first time a
    model finishes loading in a session.
  - `--num-ctx N` (CLI) and `/num-ctx [N]` (REPL) set the context window
    size. A request above the model's max context (read from `/api/show`)
    is capped to that max with a warning instead of being sent as-is.
  - 2D math layout. Display math ($$...$$, \\[...\\]) is now drawn as a real
    Unicode block -- stacked fractions with a bar, sqrt overlines, sum/prod/
    lim limits above-below, integral limits on the side, matrices, cases,
    aligned columns, \\boxed borders, \\binom, tall delimiters, accents and
    \\mathbb/\\mathcal/\\mathfrak/\\mathbf letters -- centered in cyan and
    independent of the markdown flow. Inline math is flattened to a single
    line with proper operator spacing. Anything unsupported (unknown
    environment, over-wide, over-budget) falls back to the old pylatexenc
    conversion; the parser never raises.
  - Model housekeeping. Resident models are looked up via /api/ps and unloaded
    with keep_alive=0: `/model` and `/load --model` unload the current model
    before switching, `/load SESSION` asks "load with current model or last
    model?" and unloads when the session's model wins, and leaving the REPL
    (/bye, Ctrl+D) unloads too. One-shot runs stay warm unless `--unload`;
    `--keep-loaded` disables the exit unload. Embedding models are never
    unloaded. Ctrl+C while a command prompt is open no longer kills the REPL.
  - Live tokens/s estimator. A `~42.3 tok/s · 137 tok` footer streams under
    the answer (thinking + answer chunks, 5s sliding window), with `--no-tps`,
    config `tps_footer` and `/tps on|off`.
  - Thinking is rendered like the answer (dim markdown + 2D math) and is
    scrollable: Ctrl+T (or `/thinking full`) opens the full accumulated
    thinking in the pager, then the stream resumes; an expanded preview is
    tail-capped to the terminal height and the full text is printed into
    scrollback when the answer starts.
  - Thinking renders live. The streaming view redraws on `message.thinking`
    chunks too (previously only answer chunks triggered a Live update, so a
    long chain-of-thought ran behind a blank screen), and it opens with a
    "waiting for model…" spinner so cold model loads show activity.
  - Collapsible thinking display. Default is collapsed: an animated
    "thinking · 1.2k chars · Ctrl+T to expand" spinner line while the model
    reasons, then a one-line footer above the answer. Ctrl+T expands or
    collapses mid-stream (expanded mode shows a rolling tail preview; the
    full text is kept in the session and in `--show`/exports). `--show-thinking`
    starts expanded, `--hidethinking` starts hidden, config key `thinking`.
  - New `/thinking [show|collapse|hide|toggle|full]` REPL command and the
    Ctrl+T shortcut documented in `/? shortcuts`.
  - Initial version. Drop-in superset of `ollama run MODEL [PROMPT]`: every
    ollama 0.34 flag is accepted (--dimensions, --format, --hidethinking,
    --insecure, --keepalive, --nowordwrap, --think, --truncate, --verbose),
    plus --host/-m/--system/--option/--image and session management flags
    (--continue, --resume, --session, --list, --show, --search, --export,
    --delete, --reindex) and --json/--raw scripting output.
  - Markdown rendering with Live incremental re-render while streaming;
    LaTeX math ($...$, $$...$$, \\(...\\), \\[...\\]) is converted to Unicode
    via pylatexenc (with an inline ^/_ super/subscript pass) and protected
    from code fences/spans. --render markdown|plain|raw, --no-math,
    --nowordwrap.
  - Every conversation is saved to ~/etc/data/ollamarun (one atomic JSON per
    session plus index.json): resume/continue/view/search/export (md, json,
    html) /tag/delete (via trash-put). Prompt input history is kept with
    prompt_toolkit unless OLLAMA_NOHISTORY is set.
  - Interactive REPL on prompt_toolkit: /help, /set (parameter|system),
    /show, /load, /save (creates a real Ollama model via /api/create),
    /clear, /bye, /? shortcuts -- plus /undo, /retry, /edit, /branch,
    /context, /summarize, /sessions, /title, /tag, /model, /params, /think,
    /system, /image, /render, /math, /pager, /copy, /export, /stats, /new.
    Tab completion for commands, session ids, model names and @file paths;
    Ctrl+G opens $OLLAMA_EDITOR/$EDITOR; Ctrl+C cancels a generation without
    leaving the session.
  - Vision support (--image PATH / /image PATH, persisted with the session),
    @path file mentions inlined into the prompt with a size guard, rich
    pager, /copy via pyperclip, auto titles, tags and context-window
    accounting with optional /summarize compaction.
  - Raw HTTP client (requests) so all traffic can go through llm-jukebox on
    :11434; embedding-capability models with --dimensions/--truncate route
    to /api/embed and print a vector summary (full vector with --json).

Usage:
    ollamarun MODEL [PROMPT]                 # one-shot or interactive REPL
    ollamarun                                # pick a model, start a session
    ollamarun -c                             # continue the most recent session
    ollamarun -c SESSION_ID                  # continue a specific session
    ollamarun -r                             # browse and resume sessions
    ollamarun --list                         # list saved sessions
    ollamarun --show SESSION_ID              # render a saved transcript
    ollamarun --search TEXT                  # search across sessions
    ollamarun --export SESSION_ID --export-format md --out FILE
    ollamarun --delete SESSION_ID [-y]       # move session to trash

Config: ~/etc/config_files/ollamarun.json (created with defaults on first
run). Sessions: ~/etc/data/ollamarun/sessions/<id>.json + index.json.
Prompt history: ~/etc/data/ollamarun/history. Debug log:
~/etc/logs/ollamarun.log (with --debug).

Implementation: ollamarun_lib/ (see CLAUDE.md's Architecture section).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))

from ollamarun_lib.cli import main  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
